  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 238 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nOn Monday the southern stream closed low will transition into a\nnegatively tilted more open wave and slip north into the midwest.\nSome CAPE is tucked right in the triple point, but the speed of\nthe system keeps the warm sector out of the state until the \novernight hours. CAPE will build on the warm sector of the front\nas it stalls across the middle of the state. Much of next week \nwill have split weather between the north and southern half. The\nnorthern half will have more seasonal temperatures in the low\n60s whereas 70 degree highs will be common across the south. \nRain and some thunderstorms will remain in the picture. This \npattern will remain until the east CONUS ridge is broken down by\na stronger system from the west.",
